#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# energy_function

#% text
# `energy_function(L, q, t)` gives the energy (the Jacobi integral) `sum q' dL/dq' - L` of the Lagrangian `L` in the coordinates `q`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The energy function is conserved along every solution when `L` does not depend on `t` explicitly.

#% item
# It is the Hamiltonian written in the velocities; `energy_drift` uses it to check numerical solutions.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
energy_function(m*x'(t)^2/2 - k*x(t)^2/2, x, t)
#% output
#= (1/2)*k*x(t)^2 + (1/2)*m*x'(t)^2

#% cell
energy_function(m*l^2*th'(t)^2/2 + m*g*l*cos(th(t)), th, t)
#% output
#= (1/2)*m*l^2*th'(t)^2 - g*l*m*cos(th(t))

#% text
# Conservation, checked with the equation of motion `x'' = -x^3`:

#% cell
simplify(rewrite(d(energy_function(x'(t)^2/2 - x(t)^4/4, x, t), t), x''(t) -> -x(t)^3))
#% output
#= 0

